uote spread need not be wrong or stale: quote/trade timestamps can differ. No prediction accuracy, latency, or venue-wide behavior is inferred from this unvalidated archive."},"methods":["Primary comparison fixed at one day before recorded close. Original Kalshi sample selected up to 250 contracts per horizon in a deterministic hash order independent of outcomes.","All price measures use exactly the same contract/horizon observations and original YES outcome; no favorite threshold or probability bins.","The source chooses the last active hourly candle within the preceding 24 hours with a two-sided quote strictly between zero and one.","Brier improvement = mean squared error of trade minus mean squared error of midpoint. Positive values favor midpoint. Approximate 95% Student-t intervals cluster paired residuals by parent event.","One-day analysis is primary. Other horizons and inside/outside-spread comparisons are descriptive sensitivity checks, not independent confirmations.","Bid and ask are included as quote-side diagnostic comparisons, not asserted fair probabilities or achievable net returns.","New third-party archive pinned to a repository revision; downloaded bytes hashed. Excluded missing trades, crossed books and boundary quotes. Snapshots have unique contract/time keys. No convergence-inferred labels are used to score forecasts."],"limitations":["Trade and bid/ask closes are from the same hour, not necessarily the same second. This is not a true simultaneous executable-price experiment.","Recorded close is only a proxy for the time the outcome became known. Prices can still include already-known information.","The Kalshi sample favors active markets with two-sided quotes and is small. Horizon cohorts differ. It cannot establish that spread causes forecast errors.","The third-party archive lacks event clocks and canonical parent IDs. Zero of the fixed sample of official exact-slug lookups matched; that does not prove the data false, but prevents reliable linkage.","The third-party watchlist deliberately selected active markets and rotated; observations are highly repeated and not independent. Its outcome labels are time-censored, and some were inferred from prices.","No fees, order size, slippage, fills, settlement delay or trading profitability are modeled."],"sources":[{"title":"Kalshi validated historical quote sample","url":"data/quotes/kalshi.json","sha256":"381211722aa3545e86ccfefc8153ae8015511a63bc3a20edc4320adb1818344b"},{"title":"Kalshi historical candle documentation","url":"https://docs.kalshi.com/api-reference/historical/get-historical-market-candlesticks"},{"title":"Third-party Polymarket Order Book Dataset — Dinesh Gopalakrishnan, CC BY 4.0","url":"https://github.com/DineshKumar8399/polymarket-orderbook-dataset"},{"title":"Pinned third-party watchlist recording","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/DineshKumar8399/polymarket-orderbook-dataset/resolve/3030329b2a7a58fdf93c9b2aa3c68a0848d63137/watch_quotes.parquet","sha256":"181ed3064c7471ee7a3b40daba7e078e3fed163a79128d6821df8f13c6c13ab2","revision":"3030329b2a7a58fdf93c9b2aa3c68a0848d63137"},{"title":"Pinned labels downloaded for identifier-audit sampling only; not used as forecast targets","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/DineshKumar8399/polymarket-orderbook-dataset/resolve/3030329b2a7a58fdf93c9b2aa3c68a0848d63137/labels.parquet","sha256":"d8c509016fd15ba0ac346c9b9eedd5febcaf660703093ea4a3886b87cb979dbc"},{"title":"Pinned metadata inspected for event-clock availability","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/DineshKumar8399/polymarket-orderbook-dataset/resolve/3030329b2a7a58fdf93c9b2aa3c68a0848d63137/markets.parquet","sha256":"9469b844297763fc9259a902b53df6100e0d1dd9ac95e9cdeef7dcc7e6f487c2"},{"title":"Official market identity API","url":"https://gamma-api.polymarket.com/docs"},{"title":"Official exact-slug lookup audit","url":"data/expansion/quote-identifier-audit.json","sha256":"2201117c7d39cbd4872f3fd9347c055fd789b5a9efccf222b372c0395969e62d"}